  "description": "ATOPEG crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C94 H151 Co3 Gd3 O30 P2,C5 H10 O2,C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.465-4.637 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.06-132.25°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co3Gd3(OH)2(R′PO3)2(tBuCO2)9(tBuCO2H)(H2O)2]·tBuCO2H·2CH2Cl2 (R′ = 2,7-di-tert-butyl-9-methyl-9H-fluoren-9-yl). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
